        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(synology-chat): bound outbound NAS response bodies to prevent Gateway OOM",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOutbound Synology Chat responses previously buffered response bodies without a byte cap, risking Gateway OOM within the request timeout. Inbound webhooks were already bounded.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Chatbot POST (status-only):** success follows HTTP status; unused body is destroyed/discarded without buffering so a large 200 body cannot flip a successful send into a false failure or unbounded memory growth.\n- **user_list:** keep bounded body reads (1 MiB) with cache fallback on overflow.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Current head:** `5cf15ff8`\n\n**Unit tests:**\n\n```\npnpm exec vitest run extensions/synology-chat/src/client.test.ts\n```\n\nIncludes large-body HTTP 200 status-only regression with local destroy spy (unbound-method clean).\n\n**Current-head loopback proof (redacted, local script not in diff):**\n\n```\nPROOF_HEAD=5cf15ff8 node --expose-gc --import tsx /tmp/pr105089-proof/loopback-large-200.mjs\n{\n  \"head\": \"5cf15ff80eced815db161885fa3acc804d2c9f45\",\n  \"bodyAdvertisedMiB\": 32,\n  \"sendMessageOk\": true,\n  \"elapsedMs\": 14,\n  \"serverBytesWritten\": 1572864,\n  \"serverClosedBeforeFullBody\": true,\n  \"rssMiB\": {\n    \"before\": 142.5,\n    \"after\": 142.9,\n    \"delta\": 0.4\n  },\n  \"heapUsedMiB\": {\n    \"before\": 18.5,\n    \"after\": 18.7,\n    \"delta\": 0.2\n  },\n  \"proof\": \"PASS: large HTTP 200 succeeded without response-sized buffering\"\n}\n```\n\nInterpretation:\n- Chatbot sendMessage returns true on HTTP 200 even when the NAS advertises a 32 MiB unused body.\n- Server writes about 1.5 MiB then closes early (serverClosedBeforeFullBody true) because the client destroys the unused stream.\n- RSS/heap delta on the POST path is about +0.4 / +0.2 MiB — not response-sized buffering.\n\n**Lint:** oxfmt + oxlint on touched files — clean\n\n## Review\n\n- ClawSweeper Rank-up P1 proof: current-head large HTTP 200 success without buffering (above)\n- Remaining maintainer item: confirm 1 MiB user_list envelope (owner call)\n- AI-assisted: Yes\n",
